hi this is pressure Locker in this video  we're going to evaluate whether a common  way of choosing the dealer and poker is  actually a fair system imagine we have a  poker game between four players one two  three and four  we'll deal out cards from the deck until  we see the first ace this person will be  the dealer this is a system of dealing  to the first ace but is this a fair  system let's do an experiment to find  out we'll deal out the cards and see who  gets the first ace and then we'll put a  counter next to that player we'll repeat  this experiment a hundred times and keep  track of which player was designated the  dealer using the system of dealing to  the first ace as you can tell from the  preliminary results player four gets the  first ace very few times and the earlier  players are much more favored as we do  this experiment a hundred times we see  this pattern holds true and in the end  we're going to collect the data and  analyze it if dealing to the first days  were a fair system we would expect a  uniform distribution what we found was  big variance between the players in  particular the earlier players were much  more likely to get the first ace this is  in line with the theoretical results  dealing to the first ace is not a fair  system if you want a truly fair way of  picking the dealer you can either do a  high card you can draw straws or you can  do random numbers which is what most  tournaments do please subscribe to my  channel I make videos on math and game  theory you can support mind your  decisions on patreon to get exclusive  rewards you can also catch me on my blog  minor decisions on Twitter at pressure  Locker or get my books at Amazon
 

